{"file":"perception-first-design-0.7.0-v2.zip","bytes":343102,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"perception-first-design","description":"Perception-First Design (PFD) — psychology-backed design framework. 5-layer dependency stack derives requirements from cognitive constraints before proposing solutions. Auto-activates on design, marketing, copywriting, and communication tasks.","version":"0.7.0","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","repository":"https://github.com/skovalik/perception-first-design","homepage":"https://aurochs.agency/perception-first-design","keywords":["design","ux","marketing","copywriting","conversion","psychology","cognitive-science","perception","communication"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/pfd/SKILL.md","name":"pfd","description":"This skill should be used when working on any design, marketing, copywriting, writing, or communication task — including: \"run PFD\", \"apply PFD\", \"use Perception-First Design\", \"do a PFD analysis\", \"run the derivation protocol\"; when designing interfaces, landing pages, emails, ads, or visual systems; when writing or reviewing marketing copy, headlines, CTAs, proposals, pitches, or presentations; when evaluating conversion problems, bounce rates, engagement, or persuasion; when doing brand work, content strategy, or any client communication; or whenever cognitive load, first impressions, processing fluency, trust, or decision architecture should inform the work.","headings":["Perception-First Design (PFD): v0.7.0","What PFD Is","The Three Modes","Mode Detection (Auto)","The 5-Layer Dependency Stack","Cognitive Load (L0)","Layer 1: First-Impression Architecture","Layer 2: Processing Fluency","Layer 3: Perception Bias Optimization","Layer 4: Decision Architecture","The Derivation Protocol","Step 1 — State the Design Problem","Step 2 — Work Each Layer Bottom-Up","Step 3 — Accumulate Requirements","Step 4 — Derive the Solution","Step 5 — Test Against Proposals (if any)","Step 6 — Identify the Gap","Output Closing"],"name_hint":"pfd"}],"commands":[{"path":"commands/all.md","name":"all","description":"Run all three PFD modes (analyze, solve, evaluate) on the same input. Produces three full outputs side-by-side, one per cognitive contract. Use when a question genuinely warrants multiple cognitive contracts, or when you want to see what the question reveals across descriptive, prescriptive, and rated lenses simultaneously.","headings":["PFD All: Three-Mode Composite","Input","When to use this vs. the individual modes","Process","Section 1: Analyze (descriptive)","Section 2: Solve (prescriptive)","Section 3: Evaluate (rated)","Output format"]},{"path":"commands/analyze.md","name":"analyze","description":"Analyze a hypothetical change, mechanism, or behavioral pattern with Perception-First Design. Mode 3 descriptive analysis. Walks the 5 layers as predictive lenses to enumerate cascading consequences, trade-offs, and integrative compounds. Use for \"what happens if\", \"why does X work\", \"users say X but do Y\" questions that want results, not recommendations.","headings":["PFD Analyze: Descriptive Analysis","Input","When to use this vs. solve / evaluate","Process","Step 1. Restate the question","Step 2. Walk each layer bottom-up as a descriptive lens","Step 3. Check for trade-offs","Step 4. Check for integrative compounds"]},{"path":"commands/evaluate.md","name":"evaluate","description":"Evaluate an artifact (URL, HTML, screenshot, copy) with Perception-First Design. Mode 1 corpus-backed evaluation that loads heuristic rules, design system profiles, worked examples, and the psychology corpus to produce a layered scoring with citations.","headings":["PFD Evaluate — Corpus-Backed Evaluation","Input","Process"]},{"path":"commands/solve.md","name":"solve","description":"Solve a design, marketing, writing, or communication problem with Perception-First Design. Runs the Mode 2 derivation protocol — derives requirements R1-R5 from cognitive constraints, then produces a solution that satisfies all of them.","headings":[]}],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Perception-First Design","What Changes When You Have This","The Ralph Loop","The Five Layers","Try It","For Practitioners","In Claude Code","Bare invocation — auto-detects mode from input","Force Mode 2 (solve): derives a solution from cognitive constraints","Force Mode 1 (evaluate): corpus-backed audit of an existing artifact","Force Mode 3 (analyze): descriptive cascade for hypotheticals and mechanism questions","Composite: run all three modes on the same input","Example output","Analyze (descriptive)","Solve (prescriptive)","Evaluate (rated)","What's in the Repo"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".github/FUNDING.yml",".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/design-system-profile.md",".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/framework-correction.md",".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/learning-submission.md",".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/new-heuristic-rule.md",".github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md",".gitignore","CHANGELOG.md","CITATION.cff","CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md","CONTRIBUTING.md","CONTRIBUTORS.md","LICENSE","NOTICE","README.md","commands/all.md","commands/analyze.md","commands/evaluate.md","commands/solve.md","corpus/core/anti-patterns.md","corpus/core/constitutional-constraints.md","corpus/core/output-schema.md","corpus/core/pfd-layer-rubric.md","corpus/core/psychology/mvs-psychology-reference.md","corpus/core/tier2-prompt-template.md","corpus/design-systems/web-frameworks/shopify-themes.md","corpus/design-systems/web-frameworks/tailwind.md","corpus/design-systems/web-frameworks/wordpress-themes.md","corpus/heuristics/universal/foundation-rules.yaml","corpus/heuristics/universal/l1-rules.yaml","corpus/heuristics/universal/l2-rules.yaml","corpus/heuristics/universal/l3-rules.yaml","corpus/heuristics/universal/l4-rules.yaml","corpus/worked-examples/web/example-cross-layer.md","corpus/worked-examples/web/example-excellent.md","corpus/worked-